  "note": "Yes, 6990 is the right account, so reclass the clerk's $5.70 on A-BL-00423 from 4000 to 6990. One correction: the limit is $15, not $12.28. Commercial laundry customers who short-pay by up to $15 get matched and written off to 6990, and anything bigger goes to the owner (Marv).",
  "explanation": "The controller confirmed 6990 is the right account, raised the limit to $15 and said anything over $15 goes to Marv, the owner. A-R-014 now covers commercial laundry customer shortfalls up to $15.00 (was $12.28), and A-R-015 now sends shortfalls over $15.00 to Marv (was over $12.28). The clerk's $5.70 on A-BL-00423 still needs a one-off reclass from 4000 to 6990. That's a journal entry, not a playbook rule. A-R-014 and A-R-015 still use different description patterns and search windows, so some shortfalls over $15 may not reach Marv. That hasn't been changed.",
